    FraudCheckChain o-- FraudCheck : runs in order
    FraudCheck <|.. AccountBlockedCheck
    FraudCheck <|.. VelocityCheck
    FraudCheck <|.. AmountLimitCheck
    FraudCheck <|.. DailyLimitCheck
    BillerAdapterRegistry o-- BillerAdapter : finds by biller code
    BillerAdapter <|.. ElectroCoAdapter
    BillerAdapter <|.. AquaCoAdapter
    BillerAdapter <|.. TopUpNetAdapter
    RequeryScheduler ..> PaymentOrchestrator : calls
    ReconciliationService ..> BillerAdapterRegistry : parses files
    ReconciliationService ..> PaymentOrchestrator : resolves Unknown
    RefundService ..> WalletService : pays refund
    RefundService ..> AuditService : records
    AdminService ..> AuditService : records
    SupportService ..> AuditService : records

    note for User "role CUSTOMER / AGENT / ADMIN / SUPPORT / SYSTEM.\nAdmin and Support are roles, not separate tables.\nThe SYSTEM user is seeded and owns PayLink's own wallet (fee income).\nA velocity block sets blockedUntil (10 minutes). A support block has no end time until support unblocks.\nWhile blocked, only bill payments are refused. Wallet view and top-ups still work."
    note for Wallet "Balances are computed from LedgerEntry (never overwritten), exact Decimal.\nAvailable = TOP_UP + RELEASE + REFUND + FEE_INCOME + COMMISSION - HOLD - FEE_REVERSAL - COMMISSION_REVERSAL\nHeld = HOLD - CAPTURE - RELEASE\nAmounts are stored positive. The entry type gives the sign.\nversion = optimistic lock. A row lock is also taken during the limit check and hold (hard case 4)."
    note for LedgerEntry "Unique (payment_id, wallet_id, entry_type) when payment_id is set,\nso a payment cannot be captured, released or refunded twice.\nFEE_INCOME = service fee minus commission (SYSTEM wallet).\nCOMMISSION = agent share (agent wallet).\nOn an approved refund: REFUND to the customer, COMMISSION_REVERSAL from the agent, FEE_REVERSAL from the SYSTEM wallet."
    note for Agent "Agent id = User id (agents.user_id is the PK).\ncommissionRate defaults from config AGENT_COMMISSION_RATE (0.40).\nFeeCalculator is the only place that computes commission.\nThe commission amount is stored on the Payment when it is created, so a late completion or a refund uses the same value."
    note for Payment "State transitions follow FR-11 and are checked by PaymentStateMachine.\nNo auto-refund while state is Unknown.\npaymentReference is the PayLink reference sent to the biller and used to match callbacks and settlement lines.\n5.00 to 10000.00 EGP bounds apply to totalAmount (bill + fee).\nunknownAt is the start for the 1, 5 and 15 minute re-queries. acceptedAt is the start of the 5 minute TopUpNet callback timer.\ncairoDate is the Cairo calendar day used for the daily limit."
    note for IdempotencyKey "Unique (customerId, key). The customer is the payer, even when an agent sends the request.\nKept until expiresAt (IDEMPOTENCY_RETENTION in config)."
    note for BillerCallback "Every callback is saved, including duplicates, so support can see that it was received and ignored.\nexternalEventId is NOT unique.\nA conflicting callback is flagged for review. The payment state is never changed by it."
    note for BillerAdapter "Biller Integration module. Adding a biller means adding one adapter and configuration only (NFR-4).\nElectroCo: live, confirms in the same request.\nAquaCo: live but slower, still within 10 seconds.\nTopUpNet: replies Accepted and calls back later.\nAll billers must follow the same payment life cycle."
    note for ReconciliationItem "Matched by paymentReference using the common file layout: payment reference, amount, status.\nOnly Unknown payments are resolved automatically (to Completed or Failed).\nFailed or Refunded payments listed as received are flagged only. No state or balance change."
    note for Refund "Full refunds only on Completed payments after support approval.\nThe payment stays Completed and a separate refund record plus ledger entries are created."
    note for SystemConfig "Limits, fees, velocity, timeouts, retry schedule, idempotency retention and commission values.\nEditable at runtime without redeploying (FR-24). Every change is audited."
    note for AuditService "One audit record for every money movement: top-up, hold, capture, fee credit, commission credit, release, refund.\nAlso for biller, service, fee, limit and account changes."
